From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 15:43:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda: TF_GLM_KV=fp8 on the AFD attention node
 (MiaAI-Lab recipe patch 0038, 0041's ring span)

MiaAI-Lab's recipe (github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold @ cf28cc4, KV=fp8 by
default) holds the DSA latent cache and the indexer's pooled keys as e4m3 rows with a power-of-two fp32 scale each
(width + 16 bytes a row), and the indexer's per-token keys and gates in one window-sized ring a stream slot. This
ports recipe patch 0038-glm-kv-fp8 and the ring-base span of 0041-glm-parallel-ring-base (Apache License 2.0,
Copyright 2026 MiaAI-Lab) onto the split's world-1 attention node:

- kv8.py: the recipe's file, unchanged (a two-line credit header added);
- latent.py / sparse.py: the cache kernels and their entry points are the recipe's functions, source text identical
  to the recipe's tree after 0038 (latent: _lat_write latent_write _tile _dense_chunks _sparse_chunks _lat_get
  _lat_put _seg_lat_write seg_latent_write _seg_chunks; sparse: _index_write _pool_keys index_update _scores _pk_put
  _pk_get _seg_index_write _seg_pool_keys seg_index_update _seg_scores seg_select_tokens). The launch wrappers keep
  TensorFold's settings and pass kv8.parts (attention, sparse_attention, seg_attention, select_tokens);
- segments.py, verify.py (0041's ring-base span), multi.py, forward.py (Caches: kv, rings, index_ring,
  index_tensors), decode.py (Snapshot.tail, _ring_tail, put_ring_tail), engine.py and cuda/geometry.py
  (mla_row_bytes, mla_index_ring, mla_ring_bytes; the estimate and the settings carry the kind): 0038's hunks,
  applied by hand where TensorFold differs.

Differences from the recipe, all glue:
- the rings come with TF_GLM_KV=fp8 only (the recipe uses them for every kind), so unset or bf16 keeps the caches,
  snapshots, estimate and kernel bytes exactly as before;
- decode.prefill's kept point inside a prompt chunk (keep_at, not in the recipe) copies its ring tail before the
  next chunk overwrites it; multi._keep re-takes the tail with the MTP layer's length; multi._reslot moves the
  stream's ring rows with it (the recipe's 0038 leaves them; TF_GLM_MULTI_LONE is off by default in both);
- pools are read with getattr, so a pool without rings (the multi-stream tests' pool double) is a bf16 pool.

The attention node at world 1, with and without --parallel: 6,716 B a window token instead of 18,112; q4 dense +
fp8 at --parallel 4 x 262,144 estimates 16.10 GiB of an RTX 5090's 28.75 GiB. Unset: byte-identical to before.

Tests: tests/test_glm_kv8.py, tests/test_glm_kv8_multi.py and tests/glm_kv8_cpu.py (CPU: flag-off bytes, the
recipe's kernels and bytes under Triton's interpreter against tests/data/glm_kv8_golden.json, dequantized reads,
rings, --parallel slot moves, the estimate).

Credit: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the ported files' headers name MiaAI-Lab and the patches.

